\pard\plain \s40\li0\widctlpar\adjustright \shading1000\cbpat8 \f2\fs16\cgrid 1 {\cf20 /* stb_image - v2.30 - public domain image loader - http://nothings.org/stb}\par
2 {\cf20                                   no warranty implied; use at your own risk}\par
3 {\cf20 }\par
4 {\cf20    Do this:}\par
5 {\cf20       #define STB_IMAGE_IMPLEMENTATION}\par
6 {\cf20    before you include this file in *one* C or C++ file to create the implementation.}\par
7 {\cf20 }\par
8 {\cf20    // i.e. it should look like this:}\par
9 {\cf20    #include ...}\par
10 {\cf20    #include ...}\par
11 {\cf20    #include ...}\par
12 {\cf20    #define STB_IMAGE_IMPLEMENTATION}\par
13 {\cf20    #include "stb_image.h"}\par
14 {\cf20 }\par
15 {\cf20    You can #define STBI_ASSERT(x) before the #include to avoid using assert.h.}\par
16 {\cf20    And #define STBI_MALLOC, STBI_REALLOC, and STBI_FREE to avoid using malloc,realloc,free}\par
17 {\cf20 }\par
18 {\cf20 }\par
19 {\cf20    QUICK NOTES:}\par
20 {\cf20       Primarily of interest to game developers and other people who can}\par
21 {\cf20           avoid problematic images and only need the trivial interface}\par
22 {\cf20 }\par
23 {\cf20       JPEG baseline & progressive (12 bpc/arithmetic not supported, same as stock IJG lib)}\par
24 {\cf20       PNG 1/2/4/8/16-bit-per-channel}\par
25 {\cf20 }\par
26 {\cf20       TGA (not sure what subset, if a subset)}\par
27 {\cf20       BMP non-1bpp, non-RLE}\par
28 {\cf20       PSD (composited view only, no extra channels, 8/16 bit-per-channel)}\par
29 {\cf20 }\par
30 {\cf20       GIF (*comp always reports as 4-channel)}\par
31 {\cf20       HDR (radiance rgbE format)}\par
32 {\cf20       PIC (Softimage PIC)}\par
33 {\cf20       PNM (PPM and PGM binary only)}\par
34 {\cf20 }\par
35 {\cf20       Animated GIF still needs a proper API, but here's one way to do it:}\par
36 {\cf20           http://gist.github.com/urraka/685d9a6340b26b830d49}\par
37 {\cf20 }\par
38 {\cf20       - decode from memory or through FILE (define STBI_NO_STDIO to remove code)}\par
39 {\cf20       - decode from arbitrary I/O callbacks}\par
40 {\cf20       - SIMD acceleration on x86/x64 (SSE2) and ARM (NEON)}\par
41 {\cf20 }\par
42 {\cf20    Full documentation under "DOCUMENTATION" below.}\par
43 {\cf20 }\par
