1914 {\cf20 //  "baseline" JPEG/JFIF decoder}\par
1915 {\cf20 //}\par
1916 {\cf20 //    simple implementation}\par
1917 {\cf20 //      - doesn't support delayed output of y-dimension}\par
1918 {\cf20 //      - simple interface (only one output format: 8-bit interleaved RGB)}\par
1919 {\cf20 //      - doesn't try to recover corrupt jpegs}\par
1920 {\cf20 //      - doesn't allow partial loading, loading multiple at once}\par
1921 {\cf20 //      - still fast on x86 (copying globals into locals doesn't help x86)}\par
1922 {\cf20 //      - allocates lots of intermediate memory (full size of all components)}\par
1923 {\cf20 //        - non-interleaved case requires this anyway}\par
1924 {\cf20 //        - allows good upsampling (see next)}\par
1925 {\cf20 //    high-quality}\par
1926 {\cf20 //      - upsampled channels are bilinearly interpolated, even across blocks}\par
1927 {\cf20 //      - quality integer IDCT derived from IJG's 'slow'}\par
1928 {\cf20 //    performance}\par
1929 {\cf20 //      - fast huffman; reasonable integer IDCT}\par
1930 {\cf20 //      - some SIMD kernels for common paths on targets with SSE2/NEON}\par
1931 {\cf20 //      - uses a lot of intermediate memory, could cache poorly}\par
